  new=r"""state, in paragraph 51, that upon deletion of the decryption key the encrypted data will be unintelligible, at least until the algorithm is broken, and in the same paragraph that encrypted personal data is still personal data (European Data Protection Board, 2026b). Technical impossibility cannot be invoked to justify non-compliance (paragraph 50), and an erasure request requires the data to be erased or rendered anonymous (paragraph 125). The Guidelines therefore describe what key deletion achieves without classifying it as erasure, and they hold that hashed data may likewise remain personal data.""",
